Changelog: 21-10-2026 14:25:29

Release 0.1.0.

Changelog: 21-10-2026 13:23:31

Added. mGBA Manager: Game Boy Advance games on the BC-250 with mGBA. The app installs mGBA 0.10.5, the Linux AppImage
of its GitHub release, checked against the SHA-256 it was tried with, and says when GitHub has a newer release or when
mGBA updated itself in its own window (Install puts 0.10.5 back). It finds the games in the chosen folders (.gba files,
and .zip files with one in them, told by the cartridge header and its checksum, with the game code from it) and puts
the ticked ones in Steam for Game Mode, "[GBA] Title", the artwork drawn from the app's icon. The Game Mode shortcuts
run ~/.local/bin/bc250-mgba-run, which starts mGBA full screen (-f); when Steam starts a game, a real controller is
read instead of Steam's virtual one, and on a Wayland desktop mGBA opens through XWayland so Steam's overlay works.
Not tried on the board yet: a game from Game Mode, the controllers under Steam Input.
